id: pm-lint-authoring-repair-previews
title: Preview minimal authoring repairs without writing tracker state
description: Assemble revision-bound mechanical repair patches and explicit substantive questions from lint context using core disposable mutation validation. No application or automatic acceptance authoring.
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T06:35:47.072Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T06:58:53.857Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Whitespace and duplicate-tag fixes revalidate cleanly in preview; absent expected behavior remains a question; stale revisions refuse; preview makes zero writes; typed SDK and compact TOON/JSON CLI are documented and validated on public tracker copies outside git.
parent: pm-lint-epic
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T06:35:52.306Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: inspected pm-lint diagnostics, baselines, rule packs and witnesses; core structured mutation planning and previewItemMutations; sibling pm-review lineage, pm-presets upgrade, pm-memory consolidation and pm-todos proposals. Existing facilities diagnose/acknowledge debt or validate/apply specific domains. This feature assembles bounded revision-bound mechanical repair context and explicit questions, delegates semantic validation to the pinned core SDK, and adds no application, sync, outbox, journal or automatic substantive authoring path. SDK pin remains 2026.10.20; registry observed 2026.10.25. Plan: read-only snapshots, revision-bound keys, SDK staged validation, strict CLI selections, non-git regression/property tests, byte-inventory real-data validation, targeted local checks and full npm/Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-25T06:48:55.180Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: single-target typed SDK and lint repair command; SDK-normalized title/tag patches, explicit substantive questions, raw-byte/native-field revision and context-bound plan key. Cold SDK reads were observed writing metadata caches and legacy Markdown reads can migrate storage; all reads now run in owned scratch snapshots and source fingerprints enforce zero source writes. No apply/journal/sync/shared mutable state is introduced. Focused tests passed 5/5 before the seeded model suite; adding TOON/JSON Markdown replay coverage and public-data measurements next."
  "2026-10-25T06:57:25.149Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"mechanical preview validates\" test/repairs.test.ts exits 1 separately with mechanicalRepairs returning an empty patch, with the saved-revision guard removed, and with source snapshot isolation bypassed. Failures respectively demonstrate missing mechanical fixes, missing stale refusal, and actual cold SDK cache writes. Restored implementation passes focused checks. Public main snapshots: pm-lint d9813e3 has 17 items; pm-review 24e04fc has 54 items. All 71 previews plus 71 revision rechecks preserve original names and bytes. pm-review emits one acceptance question and three missing expected-behavior questions. Sources contain zero mechanical debt; synthetic fixtures independently validate whitespace/duplicate-tag patches. Initial linked-test attempt was interrupted to correct its default 120-second budget and a permission-restoration test cleanup; final linked test uses an explicit 600-second budget. Test-result tracking is disabled, so aggregate outcomes are documented here rather than changing tracker policy."
  "2026-10-25T06:58:52.544Z",codex-agent,"Local evidence: pinned pm test --run --progress --timeout 600 passed 8/8 tests, including 500 seeded random sequences (seed 0x51a7e202), with no failures or skips. After adding explicit foreign-state coverage, the focused suite passed 8/8. Build, typecheck, lint, docstring (24 files, 91 declarations) and zero-duplication checks passed at unchanged thresholds. Public measurements: 71 items/previews and 71 exact-revision repeats, 4 substantive questions, 0 mechanical findings in untouched source data, 0 source writes; maximum receipts are 661 JSON / 620 TOON bytes. Independent mechanical, stale and zero-write behavioral reverts each fail. Packed npm/npx and native Bun/bunx acceptance now covers repair CLI and SDK. Development SDK pin remains 2026.10.20; peer/manifest minimum honestly matches required APIs. No apply/sync/journal/worker exists. Full unchanged release gates will be evidenced by CI; no merge or release is authorized."
